=== DISCLOSURE: the recomputed snr_current baseline does not reproduce 0.492/-0.804 ===
  Tried and all disagree with 0.492/-0.804, investigated before reporting further:
    - row-level n_discovered>=80 (band 80-100): median snr_current ~0.15
    - episode-level 'reaches n_discovered>=80 at any point': median snr_current ~0.18
    - binning by n_discovered, n_discovered_h1, n_discovered_h2 instead of n_discovered(=h3): slopes -0.36 to -0.72, none near -0.804
    - fitted-curve value at n=100 from the median-bin OLS (vs a raw sub-population median): 0.12-0.19, not 0.492
  All of these land in a consistent ~0.12-0.21 range, well below the reported 0.492, across every
  reasonable variant tried. This is NOT explained by the amendment 3 pooling bug (point slopes
  don't depend on episode identity) and is NOT resolved by any n_discovered-binning choice tried.
  Task W's OWN numerator-only slopes (-0.891/-0.988) DID reproduce closely (Amendment 4, above),
  confirming the dataset and general row-selection are right -- the gap is specific to reproducing
  the SNR RATIO's own baseline figure, not the underlying data or the general approach.
  Reported as an unresolved discrepancy, not glossed over. snr_abs below is computed on the same
  best-effort population as this non-reproducing snr_current baseline, so the ABS-vs-CURRENT
  comparison (the actual point of this task) is still internally consistent even though neither
  matches the thesis's exact reported number.

